course: dictionary
lesson: 6107
title: Mic: a short word for microphone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Then Ollie forgot his mic was on.» A mic is short for microphone, a device that picks up sound. The clue is «forgot his mic was on»: Ollie's device was switched on, so people could hear him when he did not want them to.
explain: Mic is informal, so you will hear it in chatty speech, at assemblies, on video calls and in games. Context helps: «Is your mic on?» asked on a video call means the sound device, not something you wear.
explain: Mic can also be a verb. To mic someone up means to put a microphone on them. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is someone doing something with it?
fact: Mic is short for microphone.
fact: «Mic» is informal, so it is used in everyday talk rather than formal writing.
fact: As a verb, to mic someone up means to put a microphone on them.
fact: «Mic drop» means finishing with a clever line.
fact: «You're on mute — turn your mic on» means your sound is switched off, so you need to switch it back on to be heard.
exercise: «Then Ollie forgot his mic was on.» What is a mic? | *A device that picks up sound | A small light that glows at night | A type of hat worn in the rain | A bag for carrying books
exercise: On a video call, a teacher asks, «Is your mic on?» What is she asking? | Whether you have finished your homework | Whether you are wearing a hat | *Whether your sound device is switched on
exercise: Mic is an informal word. Where would you most likely hear it? | *In chatty talk, like at a concert or in a game | In a formal letter to the headteacher | In a science textbook about rocks
test: «They mic'd up the speaker before the show.» What does mic'd up mean here? | *To put a microphone on someone | To write a speech | To turn the lights off | To wash the speaker's clothes
test: After a clever last line, a pupil says, «Mic drop!» What does it mean? | Going to bed early | Asking for a louder sound | *Finishing with a clever line | Dropping a microphone on the floor by accident
exam: Which sentence uses mic as a verb? | Is your mic on? | *Please mic up the singer before she sings. | She sang into the mic at the assembly. | The mic was broken after the concert.
